     quote         : “The third figure has not come back. We also removed a 'five-year topline of 20 January 2026' reporting a one-sided nominal p = 0.0075. That document is still in nothing we hold and in no source list on this page, and nothing found since has changed that.”
     but           : The January 20, 2026 Moderna/Merck press release is publicly available (Moderna IR PDF, s2.q4cdn.com) and reports 'one-sided nominal p=0.0075' for the five-year KEYNOTE-942 RFS analysis. CancerNetwork also cites this p-value from the five-year data. The document exists and is findable; the draft's correction notice implies it may not.
