  What this piece can add that careful coverage does not:
     No outlet found — including the most careful specialist treatments — explains the OS confidence interval (0.165–1.345) in terms of what its two ends mean in plain language, or connects the n=14 death count to the interval width in a way a non-specialist reader can use. The draft's walk-through of that interval, and its explanation of why 'an encouraging trend' is the only honest label for a result that spans an 84% reduction to a 35% increase, is genuinely absent from all coverage found and is the layer this piece adds that even the best specialist reporting does not.

